  "key_concepts": [
    "Particles are emitted from input geometry points, and initial velocity comes from point normals.",
    "Velocity, life, age, id, mass, drag, and related particle attributes must persist through the SOP chain for later simulation steps.",
    "Optional external, force, metaball, and surface-attractor inputs can alter the simulation beyond the source geometry.",
    "Modern large particle systems should usually prefer POPs or GPU-friendly workflows over the legacy CPU Particle SOP."
  ]
